# Secrets that harness tools need. The user copies this to ~/.config/harness/.env (or sets HARNESS_ENV_FILE)
# and fills in the values. The real file is never in a repo and an agent never reads it (SEC.2); the wrapper
# scripts read it themselves. An agent reads only this example, to tell the user which variable is missing or
# expired and how to renew it.

# sn-get.sh and sn-access-check.sh. A sub-prod ServiceNow instance (UAT or DEV), and an integration user with
# read ACLs on the configuration tables only ("Web service access only", not admin). Host name only, no https://.
SN_INSTANCE=
SN_USER=
SN_PASSWORD=

# sonar-read.sh. SonarCloud > My Account > Security > Generate Token (user token, expires; renew when the
# wrapper reports HTTP 401). A user token inherits your permissions, so it is not read-only by itself.
SONAR_TOKEN=
SONAR_ORGANIZATION=teamvalue
